Splitting a bill.

The share of a bill (money) among some people (a whole number) is money:
the bill divided by the people rounded to 2 places.

The share with tip of a bill (money) among some people (a whole number) is money:
the share of the bill times 1.1 among the people.

For example, the share of 90 among 3 is 30.
For example, the share of 10 among 3 is 3.33.
For example, the share with tip of 100 among 4 is 27.5.
